   7:     TDF 300 mg       ACTIVE_COMPARATOR      <- the comparator the review is named for
   8:     Open-label TAF   EXPERIMENTAL           <- the open-label extension
   9: 
  10: The object stored `TAF 25 mg` against `Open-label TAF` -- THE TWO EXPERIMENTAL ARMS -- and
  11: dropped the ACTIVE_COMPARATOR entirely. So the served pooled `OR 0.913 (0.691-1.206)` compares
  12: TAF AGAINST TAF. Worse than a wrong comparator: the open-label extension enrols EVERYONE WHO
  13: COMPLETED THE DOUBLE-BLIND PERIOD, so it contains the TDF patients who rolled over and largely
  14: the same people as the arm it is compared with.
  15: 
  16:     A CONTROL ARM THAT IS NOT A CONTROL. The number is not a weak comparison or a mismatched
  17:     one; it is not a comparison. And nothing about it looks wrong: 0.91 with a CI spanning 1 in
  18:     a head-to-head of two tenofovir prodrugs is exactly what a reader would expect to see.
  19: 
  20: AND THE DASHBOARD SERVES IT WHILE BEING UNABLE TO CHECK IT. The row for this page carries
  21: `pooled_OR: 0.912997` and `ssot_state: UNMAPPED` -- PAGE_MAP has no entry, so the projection
  22: gate that exists to stop exactly this could not see the row. The gate's own output says the
  23: unmapped rows are "uncheckable, never clean", and there are 601 of them serving a value, 562
  24: with a page on disk. This is one of them, now mapped.
  25: 
  26: THIRD: `estimand_established: true` SITTING ON TOP OF A REASON THAT SAYS IT IS NOT. The object's
  27: own `poolable_reason` reads "The extractor recovered a pooled result from this page ... Whether
  28: they SHOULD have been pooled is not established by conversion". A boolean asserting the opposite
  29: of the prose beside it.
  30: 
  31: FOURTH, AND IT IS MINE: THE QUESTION PACKETED BECAUSE OF MY OWN TOKEN FILTER. The restatement
  32: script required topic tokens longer than three characters, so `taf` and `tdf` -- the entire
  33: subject of this review -- were discarded, no coded intervention matched, and the topic was
  34: routed for escalation. THE DRUG NAME WAS TOO SHORT FOR THE FILTER. And the question was
  35: derivable all along from a field the coded-fields route never reads: the registrations'
  36: `officialTitle`, which states in plain words "Study to Compare Tenofovir Alafenamide (TAF)
  37: Versus Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate (TDF)".
